  "_commit": {
    "id": "91f71090fbbc591af8145d4c9a020d1b7b184c47",
    "author": "Eric Davis <ericscottdavis@outlook.com>",
    "committer": "Eric Davis <ericscottdavis@outlook.com>",
    "message": "Correct the note on why cooler fixtures are synthetic\n\nThe ExperimentHub records for marinerData's .cool/.mcool files do exist --\nEH9511 through EH9514, pointing at doi:10.5281/zenodo.10906240. I had stated\nthey were never published, which was wrong.\n\nThe actual gap is narrower: marinerData builds its accessors in .onLoad from\ninst/extdata/metadata.csv, and those four rows were never pushed to\nBioconductor. So the data is served but unreachable through the documented\nAPI, and the accessors the branch's tests called do not exist in any\ninstallable marinerData.\n\nThe reason for using synthetic fixtures is unchanged, and does not actually\ndepend on that: they keep R CMD check off the network and let the tests\nassert on known counts.\n",
    "time": 1785007802
  },
